  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing life-saving humanitarian protection and health care assistance to migrants and other vulnerable individuals in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon&#x2019;s crisis has increased needs among vulnerable migrants, who face greater protection risks and economic hardship. The objective of the project is to improve access to lifesaving protection and health-care services for migrants. The project continues IOM&#x2019;s efforts to mitigate the impact of socioeconomic and humanitarian crises on the protection environment for migrants, including but not limited to unaccompanied and separated children and victims of human trafficking. The project&#x2019;s main focus is on Beirut and Mount Lebanon, given IOM migrant presence monitoring indicates the highest migrant population densities in these areas. However, the project is also targeting beneficiaries countrywide.</narrative>
  </description>
